1
00:00:02,604 --> 00:00:06,709
[Subtitles by danielsangeo]

2
00:00:08,143 --> 00:00:08,577
What?

3
00:00:09,311 --> 00:00:10,012
What's going on?

4
00:00:10,412 --> 00:00:12,614
I-I fe...I feel weird.

5
00:00:12,614 --> 00:00:14,583
I don't trust these Doritos.

6
00:00:14,583 --> 00:00:16,752
I think I've got bad nachos.

7
00:00:16,752 --> 00:00:17,987
How does this happen?

8
00:00:17,987 --> 00:00:21,857
There should be enough preservatives
in these things to mummify a small dog.

9
00:00:21,857 --> 00:00:24,626
I need to find a phone
so I can call their hotline.

10
00:00:24,626 --> 00:00:26,762
Tell 'em I've got bad nachos.

11
00:00:26,762 --> 00:00:29,498
And the building's
being attacked by aliens.

12
00:00:29,498 --> 00:00:31,667
Eh, I'll just stick with nachos.

13
00:00:32,534 --> 00:00:34,970
Man, I'm getting déjà vu.

14
00:00:34,970 --> 00:00:36,205
Where am I going?

15
00:00:36,972 --> 00:00:39,341
Well, there can't be
anything good in that office

16
00:00:39,341 --> 00:00:41,610
if that guy was diving out of
the window.

17
00:00:41,610 --> 00:00:43,979
I guess that means I have to
take the elevator.

18
00:00:45,547 --> 00:00:48,917
I guess that means I have to
take the elevator!

19
00:00:48,917 --> 00:00:50,452
God dammit.

20
00:00:50,452 --> 00:00:53,355
This is exactly why you have stairs!

21
00:00:53,355 --> 00:00:55,624
Stairs without turret guns!

22
00:00:55,624 --> 00:00:57,793
Now why is there no ladder here?

23
00:00:57,793 --> 00:00:59,895
The other shaft had a ladder here.

24
00:00:59,895 --> 00:01:01,430
It was progressive.

25
00:01:01,430 --> 00:01:03,465
Well, there's a ladder on the other side.

26
00:01:03,465 --> 00:01:06,802
Oh, it's some sort of new age
Chutes and Ladders design.

27
00:01:08,837 --> 00:01:12,274
So, my only way out of here is
to take some flying leap of faith.

28
00:01:12,274 --> 00:01:15,277
Like that scene in
Indiana Jones and the Last Crusade.

29
00:01:15,277 --> 00:01:18,480
Then claw like a mad cat
and hope like hell,

30
00:01:18,480 --> 00:01:21,483
I get a grip, and don't break my ribs.

31
00:01:21,483 --> 00:01:24,119
Once again, I need a grappling hook.

32
00:01:24,119 --> 00:01:25,587
I can't believe this.

33
00:01:25,587 --> 00:01:28,123
Why do you have a ladder
in an elevator shaft?

34
00:01:28,123 --> 00:01:29,591
To fix the elevator.

35
00:01:29,591 --> 00:01:31,026
How do you get to the ladder?

36
00:01:31,026 --> 00:01:33,128
You take the elevator that doesn't work!

37
00:01:33,128 --> 00:01:34,663
Who thought this one up?!

38
00:01:34,663 --> 00:01:36,298
Jesus Christ!

39
00:01:37,299 --> 00:01:40,836
I suppose I could do the math on
whether this jump is feasible or not,

40
00:01:40,836 --> 00:01:44,039
but, y'know, I'll have plenty of
time for that when I'm dead.

41
00:01:46,608 --> 00:01:47,342
Urf.

42
00:01:47,342 --> 00:01:49,144
OH MY GOD!

43
00:01:49,144 --> 00:01:50,479
That was stupid!

44
00:01:50,479 --> 00:01:52,848
Why do I keep doing stupid things?

45
00:01:52,848 --> 00:01:54,950
Oh my God...oh...

46
00:01:54,950 --> 00:01:56,485
I could've died!

47
00:01:56,485 --> 00:02:00,522
SCIENTIST: I...I...can't
hold on...much longer...

48
00:02:00,522 --> 00:02:02,157
Oh, cry me a river!

49
00:02:02,157 --> 00:02:06,795
I just jumped across an elevator shaft
onto a ladder, and I'm still here!

50
00:02:06,795 --> 00:02:08,864
Do I look like Spiderman to you?

51
00:02:08,864 --> 00:02:12,101
No!  If I was Spiderman, I could
do that web-flinging crap

52
00:02:12,101 --> 00:02:14,069
and have been out of here hours ago.

53
00:02:14,069 --> 00:02:16,438
The point is, you can learn
how to do a pull-up.

54
00:02:17,506 --> 00:02:19,908
Although, I'll admit, these ledges suck.

55
00:02:19,908 --> 00:02:21,643
I don't understand how--Whoa!

56
00:02:21,643 --> 00:02:22,377
You might want to g--

57
00:02:22,377 --> 00:02:23,545
[scientist screams]

58
00:02:23,545 --> 00:02:24,646
[thud]

59
00:02:24,646 --> 00:02:25,514
Never mind.

60
00:02:26,448 --> 00:02:29,885
But yeah, I don't understand why
these ledges are so damned small.

61
00:02:29,885 --> 00:02:32,621
There's like just enough
room to inch along here.

62
00:02:32,621 --> 00:02:35,157
These things are designed
for Oompa Loompas.

63
00:02:35,157 --> 00:02:37,626
I bet that's how management
thinks the elevators run.

64
00:02:37,626 --> 00:02:39,561
A bunch of Oompa Loompas inside the shaft,

65
00:02:39,561 --> 00:02:41,930
singing while they move ropes and pulleys.

66
00:02:41,930 --> 00:02:54,109
[whistles Oompa Loompa song]

67
00:02:54,109 --> 00:02:56,912
What the hell, what the hell,
what the hell...?

68
00:02:56,912 --> 00:03:00,215
These ledges don't even reach the
floor the elevator's stopped on.

69
00:03:00,215 --> 00:03:02,017
What's the point of even having them?

70
00:03:02,017 --> 00:03:04,052
And why are they sloped downward?

71
00:03:04,052 --> 00:03:07,956
As the professor showed us, it's easy
enough to die without the extra help.

72
00:03:07,956 --> 00:03:08,924
Like this!

73
00:03:09,691 --> 00:03:10,359
[exhale]

74
00:03:10,592 --> 00:03:12,327
Huhh...thank you for not collapsing.

75
00:03:12,327 --> 00:03:14,129
Though, I can't say I was
too worried about that,

76
00:03:14,129 --> 00:03:16,965
seeing as how the other guy was
doing a flexed-armed hang here

77
00:03:16,965 --> 00:03:18,333
for at least five minutes.

78
00:03:18,333 --> 00:03:19,668
What was he doing there?

79
00:03:20,769 --> 00:03:22,237
Is anyone hiding up there?

80
00:03:22,504 --> 00:03:23,038
No...

81
00:03:23,772 --> 00:03:24,173
Well....

82
00:03:28,510 --> 00:03:30,179
Eh, too bad nobody's inside.

83
00:03:30,179 --> 00:03:32,714
I bet I would've scared
the crap out of them.

84
00:03:32,714 --> 00:03:35,817
Okay, this door better open or
else I'm going to kill somebody.

85
00:03:36,351 --> 00:03:37,452
All right!

86
00:03:37,452 --> 00:03:40,355
Now, nobody needs to die unless
I think of another reason.

87
00:03:40,355 --> 00:03:44,860
Oh, I like this solid hallway
with no ledges.

88
00:03:46,195 --> 00:03:50,098
Y'know, I think I just don't
feel like climbing anymore.

89
00:03:50,098 --> 00:03:52,734
SCIENTIST: For God's sake!
Open the silo door!

90
00:03:52,734 --> 00:03:53,735
SCIENTIST: They're coming for us!
What's going on?

91
00:03:53,735 --> 00:03:55,237
SCIENTIST: It's our only way out!

92
00:03:55,237 --> 00:03:57,439
SCIENTIST: Oh my God, we're doomed!
Yeah! Kick his ass!

93
00:03:57,439 --> 00:03:58,740
No, you're doing it wrong!

94
00:03:58,740 --> 00:03:59,908
[explosion]
Huh?

95
00:04:00,909 --> 00:04:02,177
Yeah!  Shoot it!

96
00:04:04,446 --> 00:04:05,647
Aww...

97
00:04:05,647 --> 00:04:08,383
You people never fail
to disappoint me.

98
00:04:08,383 --> 00:04:12,354
Why was that guy screaming about
the silo door?  It's closed.

99
00:04:12,354 --> 00:04:14,389
Well, that shotgun's mine.

100
00:04:15,290 --> 00:04:16,992
Oh, come ON!

101
00:04:16,992 --> 00:04:19,761
There's extra ammo there and everything.

102
00:04:19,761 --> 00:04:22,030
Well, I guess out of the whole facility,

103
00:04:22,030 --> 00:04:26,301
the security station is the one place
that should have bulletproof glass.

104
00:04:26,301 --> 00:04:29,738
But still, I could argue that I
have more need for a shotgun now

105
00:04:29,738 --> 00:04:31,740
than any other time in my life.

106
00:04:31,740 --> 00:04:34,309
Though, it wouldn't be the first
time I've said that.

107
00:04:34,309 --> 00:04:35,677
Why is this guy dead?

108
00:04:35,677 --> 00:04:37,145
He wasn't dead a minute ago.

109
00:04:37,145 --> 00:04:40,249
He was screaming about silo
doors like a possessed farmer.

110
00:04:40,249 --> 00:04:41,416
Did the laser kill him?

111
00:04:41,416 --> 00:04:43,018
Are these death lasers?

112
00:04:43,018 --> 00:04:46,321
They can't be that potent; his
body's not on fire.

113
00:04:46,321 --> 00:04:47,155
I'm going to touch it.

114
00:04:47,756 --> 00:04:48,590
[chirping sound]

115
00:04:48,590 --> 00:04:50,325
[whistling sound]
Well, that didn't hurt.

116
00:04:50,325 --> 00:04:51,493
[turret beeping]
What's going on?

117
00:04:51,493 --> 00:04:53,328
[turret firing]
Ah-ah!

118
00:04:53,328 --> 00:04:54,263
[turret beeping]
Of course!

119
00:04:54,263 --> 00:04:56,064
[turret beeping]
A machine-gun turret.

120
00:04:56,064 --> 00:04:57,432
[turret beeping]
Silly me, I forget how

121
00:04:57,432 --> 00:04:58,967
[turret beeping]
we need these things.

122
00:04:58,967 --> 00:05:00,135
[turret firing]

123
00:05:00,135 --> 00:05:01,870
[turret beeping]
Yep, somewhere some manager's

124
00:05:01,870 --> 00:05:03,071
[turret beeping]
feeling like less of a man

125
00:05:03,071 --> 00:05:04,806
[turret beeping]
unless he buys more turret guns.

126
00:05:04,806 --> 00:05:05,807
[turret beeping]

127
00:05:05,807 --> 00:05:06,875
[turret firing]

128
00:05:06,875 --> 00:05:07,976
[turret beeping]
Ow!

129
00:05:07,976 --> 00:05:09,978
[turret beeping]
I can't even see what I'm shooting at.

130
00:05:10,879 --> 00:05:13,915
[turret firing]
Ow!  Shit!  Fuck!

131
00:05:13,915 --> 00:05:15,717
[turret beeping]
This is worse than paintball!

132
00:05:15,717 --> 00:05:16,418
[turret beeping]

133
00:05:16,418 --> 00:05:18,820
[teleportation sound]
Oh, great timing.

134
00:05:18,820 --> 00:05:20,722
[turret firing]

135
00:05:20,722 --> 00:05:22,824
[turret beeping]
Huh, well, at least it's nondiscriminatory

136
00:05:22,824 --> 00:05:24,192
[turret beeping]
in what it shoots at.

137
00:05:24,192 --> 00:05:25,193
[turret beeping]
All the more reason

138
00:05:25,193 --> 00:05:27,929
[turret beeping]
NOT TO HAVE THEM IN THE FIRST PLACE!

139
00:05:27,929 --> 00:05:30,098
[turret beeping]
Oh, and what's this?  A dead soldier!

140
00:05:30,098 --> 00:05:31,900
[turret beeping]
This is exactly what I said

141
00:05:31,900 --> 00:05:33,168
[turret beeping]
was going to happen!

142
00:05:33,168 --> 00:05:34,803
[turret beeping]
Dead rescue team!

143
00:05:36,171 --> 00:05:38,106
That'll teach you to beep at me.

144
00:05:38,106 --> 00:05:41,276
I break alarm clocks, I can break you, too.

145
00:05:41,276 --> 00:05:43,278
So, what's the story on this guy?

146
00:05:43,278 --> 00:05:46,381
Yep, deader than a dead dead guy.

147
00:05:46,381 --> 00:05:48,817
Is that an MP5?

148
00:05:48,817 --> 00:05:50,218
It is!

149
00:05:50,218 --> 00:05:51,586
Oh-ho-ho-ho-ho!

150
00:05:51,586 --> 00:05:55,457
Now I can solve up to 800
problems a minute.

151
00:05:55,457 --> 00:05:57,559
A submachine gun.

152
00:05:57,559 --> 00:05:59,861
It's not just for party tricks.

153
00:05:59,861 --> 00:06:00,729
[teleportation sound]

154
00:06:00,729 --> 00:06:02,864
Allow me to demonstrate!

155
00:06:02,864 --> 00:06:04,766
Ah-ha-ha-ha-ha...

156
00:06:04,766 --> 00:06:07,135
That's right, short controlled bursts.

157
00:06:07,135 --> 00:06:10,038
The candle that burns twice as
bright lasts half as long.

158
00:06:10,038 --> 00:06:13,141
[teleportation sound]

159
00:06:13,141 --> 00:06:15,043
Y'know, it's a marvel of science,

160
00:06:15,043 --> 00:06:17,512
but this random teleportation
thing is getting old

161
00:06:17,512 --> 00:06:19,414
[teleportation sound]
real fast.

162
00:06:20,882 --> 00:06:23,885
Jesus Christ! Just keep them
coming, why don't ya?

163
00:06:23,885 --> 00:06:25,320
Now, what is this?

164
00:06:25,320 --> 00:06:27,889
I'm not sure, but I'm finding
that crossing these lasers

165
00:06:27,889 --> 00:06:29,424
doesn't lead to anything good.

166
00:06:30,625 --> 00:06:31,626
Hup!

167
00:06:31,626 --> 00:06:32,961
And another!

168
00:06:32,961 --> 00:06:34,529
I can limbo this.

169
00:06:34,529 --> 00:06:36,765
I thought I shouldn't be able to
see the laser beam;

170
00:06:36,765 --> 00:06:38,767
it had to be smoky or something.

171
00:06:38,767 --> 00:06:39,401
Hm.

172
00:06:39,401 --> 00:06:41,236
Oh, goodie.  Another dead guy.

173
00:06:41,236 --> 00:06:43,271
I'd better conserve on the MP5.

174
00:06:43,271 --> 00:06:44,005
[teleportation sound]

175
00:06:44,005 --> 00:06:45,640
[vortigaunt charging up]
C'mon!

176
00:06:45,640 --> 00:06:47,342
[vortigaunt bolt]
[shuddering]

177
00:06:47,342 --> 00:06:48,143
Fucker...

178
00:06:48,910 --> 00:06:49,778
[vortigaunt charging up]

179
00:06:51,546 --> 00:06:53,915
P.A.: Turret maintenance team to

180
00:06:53,915 --> 00:06:55,717
Central Command and
Communication Center.

181
00:06:55,717 --> 00:06:56,518
Ah-ha-ha-ha.

182
00:06:56,518 --> 00:06:57,586
[vortigaunt charging up]
Hey!

183
00:06:58,787 --> 00:07:02,290
I think that intercom said
'Turret maintenance to center command'.

184
00:07:02,290 --> 00:07:05,093
Yeah, I bet they have a few
questions to answer.

185
00:07:05,093 --> 00:07:08,830
Like, why are our turret guns
killing off everyone in the building?

186
00:07:08,830 --> 00:07:11,466
Man, they knew what they were
doing when they built this suit.

187
00:07:11,466 --> 00:07:14,903
I must've taken a dozen bullets
and it hasn't even punctured it.

188
00:07:14,903 --> 00:07:17,539
I'm really wishing I'd found that helmet.

189
00:07:17,539 --> 00:07:20,108
Okay, let's NOT trip this laser.

190
00:07:21,276 --> 00:07:23,745
[teleportation sound]
No!  Shut up, shut up, shut up!

191
00:07:23,745 --> 00:07:25,747
Stay on your side of the line!

192
00:07:25,747 --> 00:07:28,683
My roommate in college
used to do the same thing.

193
00:07:28,683 --> 00:07:30,485
[teleportation sound]
If I had a gun then, I'd--

194
00:07:30,485 --> 00:07:32,120
What did I just say?!

195
00:07:33,121 --> 00:07:33,922
Huh?!

196
00:07:33,922 --> 00:07:34,756
[vortigese]

197
00:07:34,756 --> 00:07:37,125
That's right!  Stay on your side.

198
00:07:37,125 --> 00:07:41,129
Your side is the one where everyone
 is dead and there are no exits.

199
00:07:41,129 --> 00:07:46,435
My side is the one filled with
hope, love and submachine guns.

200
00:07:46,435 --> 00:07:47,969
And cargo hooks.

201
00:07:47,969 --> 00:07:49,604
All right, is anyone looking?

202
00:07:49,604 --> 00:07:50,839
Okay, here we go.

203
00:07:50,839 --> 00:07:54,776
[Tarzan yell]

204
00:07:54,776 --> 00:07:55,677
[teleportation sound]

205
00:07:55,677 --> 00:07:56,311
[headcrabs squeal]
Oh, c'mon!

206
00:07:56,311 --> 00:07:58,680
Why'd you have to spoil the moment?

207
00:07:58,680 --> 00:07:59,648
[growls]

208
00:08:00,148 --> 00:08:02,818
YOU GUYS HAVE NO APPRECIATION FOR ART!

209
00:08:03,351 --> 00:08:04,686
[teleportation sound]

210
00:08:04,686 --> 00:08:05,287
CRITIC!

211
00:08:06,521 --> 00:08:08,790
You know, we're the ones
that invented teleporters...

212
00:08:08,790 --> 00:08:09,891
...I think.

213
00:08:09,891 --> 00:08:13,628
The least you could do is show a
little appreciation around here.

214
00:08:13,628 --> 00:08:18,366
Yuck, I hate to say it, but with all
these sentry guns and laser tripwires,

215
00:08:18,366 --> 00:08:22,003
I can't shake the feeling that
I'm going the wrong way again.

216
00:08:22,003 --> 00:08:25,874
I mean, let's face it: you don't put
turret guns in the visitor's center.

217
00:08:25,874 --> 00:08:26,808
Or the labs.

218
00:08:26,808 --> 00:08:29,644
Or any other place you
want people to stay alive.

219
00:08:29,644 --> 00:08:32,481
Isn't that the point of hiring
security guards?

220
00:08:32,481 --> 00:08:35,550
They're smart enough to know not
to shoot everyone?

221
00:08:35,550 --> 00:08:38,820
The crazy thing is, I may have been
doing the right thing all along.

222
00:08:38,820 --> 00:08:41,456
That turret gun must have mowed
down that soldier.

223
00:08:41,456 --> 00:08:44,459
I would've been waiting for a
rescue team that wasn't gonna make it.

224
00:08:44,459 --> 00:08:46,094
Whoa, this is slick.

225
00:08:46,094 --> 00:08:48,196
It's like there's oil mixed in
or something.

226
00:08:48,196 --> 00:08:49,030
Whoa...

227
00:08:51,666 --> 00:08:52,934
Oh, oh, nice.

228
00:08:52,934 --> 00:08:55,770
Have an empty elevator shaft for
me to slide my ass into

229
00:08:55,770 --> 00:08:58,273
after hopping over another tripwire.

230
00:08:58,273 --> 00:08:59,140
That's great.

231
00:09:00,942 --> 00:09:04,579
Oh, I see.  That was just one
stage of trying to kill me.

232
00:09:05,313 --> 00:09:06,014
SCIENTIST: Hello there.

233
00:09:06,581 --> 00:09:08,483
Uh... hi.

234
00:09:08,483 --> 00:09:10,118
Little busy here.

235
00:09:10,118 --> 00:09:12,654
Don't try to help me or anything.

236
00:09:12,654 --> 00:09:14,256
'cuz nobody does that.

237
00:09:15,123 --> 00:09:16,057
SCIENTIST: I'll stay here.

238
00:09:16,057 --> 00:09:17,058
You do that!

239
00:09:18,059 --> 00:09:20,495
God, you two are creeping me out.

240
00:09:20,495 --> 00:09:25,967
"Come play with us, Gordon.
Forever...and ever...and ever..."

241
00:09:25,967 --> 00:09:28,236
SCIENTIST: Do you know who ate
all the doughnuts?

242
00:09:28,236 --> 00:09:29,604
"The doughn--"?  No!

243
00:09:29,604 --> 00:09:32,240
I have more important things on my mind.

244
00:09:32,240 --> 00:09:33,708
Okay, this is weird.

245
00:09:33,708 --> 00:09:35,677
I'm going to need a
minute to think about this.

246
00:09:37,879 --> 00:09:42,617
SCIENTIST: Fascinating!  I never
suspected such things could be.

247
00:09:42,617 --> 00:09:43,952
Quit staring at me!

248
00:09:44,886 --> 00:09:46,100
Yeah, you!

